  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 16534a75f7 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures unless marked code read). CURRENT, WIDER. Python: run_check() -> subprocess.check_output, run_plain() -> subprocess.run, main calls both; `slice --entry main --io-boundary subprocess` reports '1 edge(s) reach this boundary' (subprocess.run only), exit 0, no warning (reproduced independently twice); --io-boundary ipc_recv keeps only check_output; io-boundaries lists check_output under both. JS: --io-boundary navigation_read keeps window.name and drops document.location. Refs: filter cli.py:1844-1847; scalar written io_boundary.py:5938, list :5955; the io-boundaries command fans out over the list at :4372; first-declared-wins loop :1632 (rationale :266-271); the --help example (cli.py:10694-10702) uses subprocess, the failing case. Scope: 41 two-boundary primitives (24 ipc_recv+subprocess, 6 env_read+navigation_read, 3 host_info_read+subprocess, 3 fs_write+subprocess, 2 fs_read+fs_write, 2 net_send+net_recv, 1 fs_read+logging); --io-boundary subprocess misses 30; the fs_write, net_recv and logging filters are affected too. Fix: read meta io_boundaries the way io_boundary.py:4372 does. P3 -> P2: a user-facing filter silently drops results."  # fc84
